and $T(j)=-i+j,$ we can draw the image of the square under the transformation $T:$\n\n![](images/ce/cee26b17d477344e138c3d6d9228f23d67c4c78ce447b1c2c3a887b79125ee7a.png)\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ represents a horizontal shear with a shear factor of $-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402588 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03061225-179d-5595-8b56-b7d6f2d13215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{3}$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402590} {:answer/id #uuid "a674a2bd-163e-5ad8-b61d-3081527c6933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402591} {:answer/id #uuid "7282a493-7961-561e-9ff5-6f77e37d9805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $3$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402592} {:answer/id #uuid "03597655-1b81-562c-95ee-e8102a15928e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402593} {:answer/id #uuid "30627c9d-0160-5ed5-9e1b-4c1eae7cdbc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $3$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $3$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402592} :answer-field/id #uuid "86c45944-9a15-5a38-bc56-297085d279dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402589}] :question/id #uuid "f8007798-26fd-5f48-9d8f-a07b9c92e47f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38020" :question/problem "Consider the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ of $\\,{R}^{2}.$ If $T$ is a linear transformation such that $T(i)=i$ and $T(j)=3j,$ then what is the geometric interpretation of the transformation $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the unit square spanned by the vectors $\\,i\\,$ and  $\\,j.$\n\n![](images/f2/f2438da7f6f0a2ab7e6653cad7776ef7d01faba55d22a480a98c152e81f0d78a.png)\n\nNow, using the fact that $T(i)=i$ and $T(j)=3j,$ we can draw the image of the square under the transformation $T:$\n\n![](images/86/8674e7345c903bf193e09cc9ae1702383cad10ba06c5dc3b6d2713ea30eb843e.png)\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch with a scale factor $3$ in the $y$-direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cbca2a4-5302-5621-923e-847f18587e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404172} {:answer/id #uuid "686c83f8-b2ff-5446-a69b-a6dca4ee631b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404173} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e87b1e-635e-59bb-a8b0-e23b7a0b0aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $2$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404174} {:answer/id #uuid "1c87caa4-7f94-5398-b1e3-967d57492e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404175} {:answer/id #uuid "2280b79f-4cae-53e8-ad6b-44654f7eae72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404175} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2dd7953-8b90-52cd-be66-71f8f16406ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404171}] :question/id #uuid "5883242f-b44f-5ff7-9fa7-30bcd180241a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81324" :question/problem "Consider the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ of ${R}^{2}.$ If $T$ is a linear transformation such that $T(i)=\\frac{1}{2}i$ and $T(j)=j,$ then what is the geometric interpretation of the transformation $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the unit square spanned by the vectors $i$ and  $j.$\n\n![](images/34/34c82826da26290fc890671734c354fbfd9c253f1cfaca38de1ea615434e6766.png)\n\nNow, using the fact that $T(i)=\\frac{1}{2}i$ and $T(j)=j,$ we can draw the image of the square under the transformation $T:$\n\n![](images/02/02470083dea4808af1854e9ed88ab496828a429c593af780209d8a6d4b15a6b1.png)\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch with a scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Shear or Stretch Transformation Given the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105766 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105618 :question/id #uuid "4d800cd6-01bd-561a-97cb-1bd672c019c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-5455" :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the following matrix\n![](images/e3/e335abcb649dae3ed9ade01017a23998614c3d0ff5a0898eb9b4d657f68e8b62.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ under the action of  $\\mathbf T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=i \\\\ T(j) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=2i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *horizontal* shear with a shear factor of $2.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c36ce626-1562-51f8-b3fd-d7dc7ce8659c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b8ead8-163c-55e6-afa2-95af3681a7e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102097} {:answer/id #uuid "9095931b-ff08-5a54-a2fb-955f264244c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $10$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102098} {:answer/id #uuid "955f0cc5-43f6-5a0e-af94-704b0c7a58c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102099} {:answer/id #uuid "b0555da6-a04e-5144-979c-b0a96959fdd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $10$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102100} {:answer/id #uuid "273e7475-d054-5f26-b9f1-7bb8aa9231b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102101}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3e5573e5-02b4-5a74-83f5-8f8e0b6b8adb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e0d6486-d718-528b-bd33-68b4cd544cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $10$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396006} {:answer/id #uuid "2ec8852b-bfa4-53a1-8fe2-e8c75b78fa64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396007} {:answer/id #uuid "8c271403-1e23-550b-9359-7ec7a8d9dd0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396008} {:answer/id #uuid "1e78af7e-059a-524f-9ce9-77e30b3e4934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $10$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396009} {:answer/id #uuid "db26a554-6026-5b02-9aa7-d6f9e0ad3b18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396008} :answer-field/id #uuid "e17cbcad-7731-506c-bd2a-44566af3416a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396005}] :question/id #uuid "6ec67f6b-b339-5863-9fd2-be6322d61819" :question/math-academy-id "q-12044" :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the following matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=i \\\\ T(j) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=10i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *horizontal* shear with a shear factor of $10.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10558cb9-d3b7-5896-9954-e86c8551abcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{12}$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348590} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec017e6-7bef-5ff0-bb14-844e3e93a3c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $12$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349315} {:answer/id #uuid "968224af-804c-5416-917f-19608cb385dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $12$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349797} {:answer/id #uuid "f481c1db-f287-593f-a6e6-ccf6e9ae2aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350587} {:answer/id #uuid "f94c1fdc-70a9-5b8c-bcd7-2144a84268d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350587} :answer-field/id #uuid "2162f09c-371c-50b2-84e4-d94cf81344b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350767}] :question/id #uuid "c971f14c-4455-5076-82e3-a0ff1ee68da4" :question/math-academy-id "q-8092" :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the following matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}=i+12j \\\\ T(j) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *vertical* shear with a shear factor of $12.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "278348b3-0eb0-5bce-ad6c-486f4ab0db04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $4$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254020} {:answer/id #uuid "5026194d-22d4-511b-b853-6303f5b4feed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254367} {:answer/id #uuid "5fab1839-ee58-5ac8-837c-72451db33a99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254525} {:answer/id #uuid "6da9523a-1503-5f47-afec-619f4b066029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254643} {:answer/id #uuid "b6714dbf-8e10-5198-a8a9-c76b5ae7eb49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $4$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254643} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ce38b01-7add-5cea-a393-692a1cf67920" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256069}] :question/id #uuid "6c5fa46e-76dc-52b3-8ecb-22249e7437d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-12042" :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the following matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=i \\\\ T(j) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=4i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *horizontal* shear with a shear factor of $4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40db7cae-9316-51e2-851c-111dff27784e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $2$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349036} {:answer/id #uuid "a890ac1f-bf44-5ac0-bdf4-33e785e099ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $2$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349947} {:answer/id #uuid "b135ba96-f3c5-5207-a3c9-d7ec82c2a682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350013} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ba9c38-53a5-5008-a5fd-9de328a80833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350323} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc2df48-316a-5681-ad3b-1c22fdc4435f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $2$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349036} :answer-field/id #uuid "1add67cd-9c91-5c89-9f5f-efeab39e2b17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350756}] :question/id #uuid "486355c1-aaab-53b3-8f31-02fd1871e35f" :question/math-academy-id "q-8089" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the following matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=2i \\\\ T(j) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a stretch of scale factor $2$ in the $x$-direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fedbbfe-52e4-5191-86d8-a6cb8a427195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $5$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348723} {:answer/id #uuid "3485994a-6471-5a88-99f7-ec1f6bbb3a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348918} {:answer/id #uuid "57264c7e-7bfb-5b58-bd90-d6c855bb7d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $5$ in the $x$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349246} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff996eb-42bc-56b2-98ef-999dd09415ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349739} {:answer/id #uuid "edd6a605-e9a9-5469-9059-3317b846a296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $5$ in the $y$-direction" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348723} :answer-field/id #uuid "214dc178-e873-5596-9c82-a5599e5bf56f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350766}] :question/id #uuid "a4ea07e2-2b18-5ed4-ac42-77d3595de881" :question/math-academy-id "q-8090" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the following matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=i \\\\ T(j) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=5j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a stretch of scale factor $5$ in the $y$-direction."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Shear or Stretch Transformation Represented by a Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105767 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105619 :question/id #uuid "043f45e2-97eb-540d-af0a-b04edb9ce60a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5456" :question/problem "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet ![](images/62/6231eb09a75376d694a6f47c47cf5a26aab4a32c28b2799f7e1f0825a7017f88.png) be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}.$ What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) under the action of $\\mathbf{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "Looking at the matrix $T,$ we can see that $\\mathbf{T}$ represents a vertical shear of shear factor $-1.$ Therefore, the image of the square $R$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/2d/2d3d15c4d6b6f9e08c6fbcc35236b50dcd6cf4d09e9204e0aa255706461c3dd8.png)\n\n**Alternative method:**\n\nWe can check that the vertices of $R$ are mapped to the vertices of the parallelogram shown above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69bac3fa-d409-5c16-87b2-383423e8d754" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106304 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8018b682-c589-5580-a601-8624b30edfa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1d25632f24abfc3176f515ba41a763e166d8c9c3101d07732a1efb183a2e9d75.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103973} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3885dd-baad-55d5-82ec-17b063e1ba13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a64061e8714d38748ef4907cbdedf873355c64814ef3966d872494e84bcacfbd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103974} {:answer/id #uuid "a5da5437-75ea-5f14-a754-73d2b88cde0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52bb468dfeaae8b4c47cb08a7bb08e671e898467e4130e2e243936b599f51704.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103975} {:answer/id #uuid "d36d5844-5bb1-51d9-80bc-ec72093bc073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/48/486044d08884fec680806e58ff8b703788e39209300e404249bb918aa8dfad41.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103976} {:answer/id #uuid "f29b9a3c-e4b1-551c-b332-c48f2afd7cf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d31375955e4f1485601baf97b053d6f9484ca906f8c4834ccb4c6559dad1c6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103977}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a577d757-0f8b-59fc-b755-dc30def59f73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103972}] :question/id #uuid "75eae5dc-d18a-5d95-b206-666c0c9aafe5" :question/math-academy-id "q-38021" :question/problem "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet $T = \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T$. What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) under the action of $T$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51760ed9-a77b-5e3b-9913-7da8ed16c5ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c28fa3fbb2a164314c00c84c70348b77457f0d39bcdcc34fbabc8e51bfdc9562.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321787} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee9affe-c344-5bd8-8a34-4efeee49a288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e3/e3937e948e6778e28246b33f336cea19e9d23ead1d8dcf6d583c6e5df05557a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321895} {:answer/id #uuid "60741513-1ac4-503c-917b-27700da97d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a64061e8714d38748ef4907cbdedf873355c64814ef3966d872494e84bcacfbd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321903} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a54001-cd9a-524d-a7ce-62888c9ae368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52bb468dfeaae8b4c47cb08a7bb08e671e898467e4130e2e243936b599f51704.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322537} {:answer/id #uuid "eef8c627-b533-520e-96a5-5fd2280ea4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/104eeafc851528b17a22a683b44a9e74c83d851976c65d39c697d550f79270c3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/104eeafc851528b17a22a683b44a9e74c83d851976c65d39c697d550f79270c3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323030} :answer-field/id #uuid "23ef16f6-ef5e-5554-b924-da06c383244d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323239}] :question/id #uuid "e7b74ac9-0349-5e05-ad52-99e0f4d0d1b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-38066" :question/problem "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet $T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Looking at the matrix $T$, we can see that $T$ represents a horizontal shear of shear factor $\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore, the image of the square $R$ under $T$ is\n\n![](images/85/85ff90a404a22310659fadd3a00c58490c9745d443b180d6b509b40a5497376b.png)\n\n**Alternative method:**\n\nWe can check that the vertices of $R$ are mapped to the vertices of the parallelogram shown above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e237090-67f0-56bb-b541-ed7861a14fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fc/fcb92d172a66567277e8619839a9d3bb4288bbe225850692eeed7267ee4d1292.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321376} {:answer/id #uuid "7161c06a-97db-533a-b1ab-361d74cbec0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b8e80ca6209eeb01ddad113b796d65fc7a60e9036594759780489321091bc42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322036} {:answer/id #uuid "75674f7b-b18d-5736-afc5-8490a1169ff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/82c6d9267a249e4beb17fa30753e0c4f11cecc88a3c26289d25b02eb7ce6b850.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322062} {:answer/id #uuid "b0267d9e-6f29-531e-a32a-75d6d2e25cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52bb468dfeaae8b4c47cb08a7bb08e671e898467e4130e2e243936b599f51704.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322528} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e1c0c0-e59a-5d74-8743-d6e4d7dfb197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/59a9db0d3848f29b1e3aafe4f485a61953e7e21822bc3e5111d7aac8bc6b8993.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b8e80ca6209eeb01ddad113b796d65fc7a60e9036594759780489321091bc42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322036} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14769a9-a9a0-531e-b547-96628c8fa631" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323482}] :question/id #uuid "07438489-a477-5e24-afda-c106a60e9af2" :question/math-academy-id "q-38070" :question/problem "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet $T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) under the linear transformation $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Looking at the matrix $T$, we can see that $T$ represents a horizontal shear of shear factor $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore, the image of the square $R$ under $T$ is\n\n![](images/4b/4b6cfc485ffa74f141e3dc4b8fad61b48103808a4f4c29b2dc5180f634902c4f.png)\n\n**Alternative method:**\n\nWe can check that the vertices of $R$ are mapped to the vertices of the parallelogram shown above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f7d7305-88a5-55e4-ad56-9bab3129e0b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1d25632f24abfc3176f515ba41a763e166d8c9c3101d07732a1efb183a2e9d75.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349323} {:answer/id #uuid "6615405c-57c2-5fc7-839a-9030fded6fba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a64061e8714d38748ef4907cbdedf873355c64814ef3966d872494e84bcacfbd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349382} {:answer/id #uuid "6f55ff27-989e-547d-9c4e-d95e074cb81c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a5da4ecc4dc4cb550649d229f0c7c9d64bd713f901084a937785ea93df86eb1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349466} {:answer/id #uuid "c7795035-1017-5a3b-a88a-a438cc90f7f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52bb468dfeaae8b4c47cb08a7bb08e671e898467e4130e2e243936b599f51704.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350203} {:answer/id #uuid "fcdeac5c-ebba-5ad8-9ad2-06ee0f4f12c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9d140b11016d68a8372623e997abdc588633ee02b56a8edee61c8cb269fd4c20.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9d140b11016d68a8372623e997abdc588633ee02b56a8edee61c8cb269fd4c20.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350675} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c7a955e-272b-533b-a34c-372a5f2e831f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350761}] :question/id #uuid "242c3fdb-6547-5215-8513-7d2ae1aba6aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-81417" :question/problem "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet $T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Looking at the matrix $T$, we can see that $T$ represents a stretch in the $y$-direction of scale factor $\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, the image of the square $R$ under $T$ is\n\n![](images/7d/7d321ec7760226fbdf2c1d539f5d9da92fa27abf84a2890702273da41df75848.png)\n\n**Alternative method:**\n\nWe can check that the vertices of $R$ are mapped to the vertices of the rectangle shown above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389567 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a71980a-a780-533c-8292-ac7c714bcb68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/364633d020e330780fab5ea588cca231ecd0e3d3c8e3e5516e4d6d0d990299c0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389569} {:answer/id #uuid "30676351-f4d0-5879-a162-25816a196693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/da/dae63d7007d115438139be51862d878deadd1ed300b3b870935c2cbe44edaef3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389570} {:answer/id #uuid "bf91d35b-3b4c-5341-8e3c-574c51f569f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/46e48817af724645b2dde55f6aa55a48c44b5160de6aebec0b1da5cc7ef1e79c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389571} {:answer/id #uuid "5c0ada63-f751-502d-996f-08e36d9763eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bfdc9898972e72a5d15c8313eff3403e2ea712e2bffe52b3fd1d9fb6156b7bec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389572} {:answer/id #uuid "bb18aec9-e801-5b41-b04e-dfaa22bace09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ad/adaef18865941a58a89a221c40f8e44aa6b95def80d12a08897c7be34ae7a9aa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bfdc9898972e72a5d15c8313eff3403e2ea712e2bffe52b3fd1d9fb6156b7bec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389572} :answer-field/id #uuid "019c3753-a69c-52d8-a6b6-c6496d15982e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389568}] :question/id #uuid "80a9d60b-2d00-5629-b0f1-438f9ef2a843" :question/math-academy-id "q-165980" :question/problem "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet $T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Looking at the matrix $T$, we can see that $T$ represents a horizontal shear of shear factor $1.$ Therefore, the image of the square $R$ under $T$ is\n\n  \n\n![](images/cf/cfe398e1ab7e5b4b487671772bf4b6127e8e141b25491f96c5cc32e77869dec0.png)\n\n**Alternative method:**\n\nWe can check that the vertices of $R$ are mapped to the vertices of the parallelogram shown above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35ad3ac6-648a-5594-bcb1-e1c6cfa23bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1d25632f24abfc3176f515ba41a763e166d8c9c3101d07732a1efb183a2e9d75.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394163} {:answer/id #uuid "222c72ce-1fbf-561c-88e0-10fe8e99adb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a64061e8714d38748ef4907cbdedf873355c64814ef3966d872494e84bcacfbd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394164} {:answer/id #uuid "25424b64-9590-5703-89ba-952c8395fabf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52bb468dfeaae8b4c47cb08a7bb08e671e898467e4130e2e243936b599f51704.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394165} {:answer/id #uuid "3cef1ad9-c2db-5b41-9454-daa475d866fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a5da4ecc4dc4cb550649d229f0c7c9d64bd713f901084a937785ea93df86eb1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394166} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5661e2-607d-5c8e-9f4c-71b76bbda105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9d140b11016d68a8372623e997abdc588633ee02b56a8edee61c8cb269fd4c20.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a5da4ecc4dc4cb550649d229f0c7c9d64bd713f901084a937785ea93df86eb1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394166} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebdb8c5b-096b-57f2-b6b3-1e02772f7b4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394162}] :question/id #uuid "e7cd28c9-29e0-5184-9921-9c2ab31af8ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-81413" :question/problem "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet $T=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Looking at the matrix $T$, we can see that $T$ represents a stretch in the $x$-direction of scale factor $\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, the image of the square $R$ under $T$ is\n\n![](images/72/72c88d1df90c3462d7f1f186c06b9a7acf30c071f5ba8bbf722ee125fee0e616.png)\n\n**Alternative method:**\n\nWe can check that the vertices of $R$ are mapped to the vertices of the rectangle shown above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Square Under a Shear or Stretch Transformation"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1358 :topic/title "Shear and Stretch as Linear Transformations"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088613} :activity/id #uuid "b39e545b-c704-5c51-a08f-b593cf84145d" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088613 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088932 :tutorial/content "Similar to transformations in a vector space, we can define a transformation between two *different* vector spaces. For instance, consider the transformation that maps the vector \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nfrom $\\mathbb{R}^2$ to the vector \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x+y \\\\ x-y \\\\ 2x+2y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nin $\\mathbb{R}^3,$ which can be written as\n\n![](images/ac/ac48dfb4fa4df769cc32789336d9f76960bde087351adf44328c33ebb1c40545.svg)\n\nThe *standard matrix* of this transformation is \n\n![](images/0a/0a94602cefa1750e0833e75a9a1e368d5d4164703fc85319db56cbfc28512194.svg)\n\nRecall that a transformation $\\mathbf{T}: V \\to W$ between two vector spaces $V$ and $W$ is *linear* if for any vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1, \\mathbf{v}_2\\in V$ and any scalar $k\\in\\mathbb{R}$, the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- $\\mathbf{T}(k\\mathbf{v}_1) = k\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1)$\n\n- $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1+\\mathbf{v}_2) = \\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1)+\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_2)$\n\nIt is easy to check that if a transformation can be represented as a matrix, then it is a linear transformation. Therefore, the transformation $\\mathbf{S}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nIn general, if $V$ and $W$ are $n$-dimensional and $m$-dimensional vector spaces respectively, then the standard matrix of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}\\!: V \\!\\rightarrow W$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix $T$." :tutorial/id #uuid "e3711b4b-0eb8-52fc-9ff2-a39add91d88b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3588 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "9ccdee64-2016-5bfd-b740-4f24ecc65aa6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088628}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088614 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63a7522-8d05-5d3a-aafb-3450292f910f"} :step/id #uuid "9f12570a-5cde-507d-b907-b9ebd270aa4d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088615}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088615 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2"} :step/id #uuid "0ba80858-7db5-5080-8b69-56bd7e22d3c4"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088628 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e35b58a-530f-5b9b-8df2-eb737f8af581"} :step/id #uuid "b2afffbf-b531-52dc-97c0-6d5bd18780e4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088614}}] :activity/title "Linear Maps Between Two Different Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087963}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050252 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087753 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087569 :question/id #uuid "ae56bd17-f7f2-5c66-ac2a-663f05c6a838" :question/math-academy-id "e-5518" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8d5b37b3da99f0b93625ab8fd6ea72615da3159a8360fe267c3ae4a470fdd7af.svg)\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector ![](images/01/01841df44c0029de31dd06a446211abb0bc0f6852d7bc76797204ae1d9a71e6c.svg) we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8x-5y \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ -4x+5y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5y-8x \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ 5y-4x\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n![](images/74/74c14f8d5615c146713a3c8ed31368a9843ed06f91d88a8745adf41764f8a003.svg)\n\nFinally, $a-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63a7522-8d05-5d3a-aafb-3450292f910f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "481dfc90-1ede-5056-b426-995af541ba2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324556} {:answer/id #uuid "5502157d-bf4e-5eb1-b5c8-946f343dc6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324677} {:answer/id #uuid "a514d9f9-d1e5-5b0f-925e-f9cdcc26dd87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325374} {:answer/id #uuid "d1033371-1675-57d2-acf6-6222ea47f819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325786} {:answer/id #uuid "dcffa4c6-0d02-5376-a22b-4375ae13b5cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325899} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3f6ed9-3d9c-5b83-9add-f760b78b8daa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326294}] :question/id #uuid "5364abc3-dc71-58da-ac04-0528dba98c51" :question/math-academy-id "q-38271" :question/problem "$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}ay+2x-2z \\\\ bz-3x+cy\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x-3y-2z \\\\ -3x-y+4z\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3y+2x-2z \\\\ 4z-3x-y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-3y+2x-2z \\\\ 4z-3x+(-1)y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+c=4+(-3)+(-1)=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "198f9d3a-d8f8-5868-bb18-4cfc9f66246e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324188} {:answer/id #uuid "3a2b3a9f-6493-5123-835f-ba98095037e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324441} {:answer/id #uuid "70ba5785-c92f-59c9-a7c6-8ed80e0956be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324899} {:answer/id #uuid "95820e02-504b-5f44-acca-c46158dff008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325244} {:answer/id #uuid "f01bdb77-f3e9-5308-85c9-d286613d7118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325244} :answer-field/id #uuid "29aa0874-2f47-52c3-ba2d-b366fc704e05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326289}] :question/id #uuid "37118a2e-2a8e-5cb5-9d41-f658c8b8e89f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38272" :question/problem "$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-3x+y \\\\ ax-8y \\\\ -9x+by\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3x+y \\\\ -2x-8y \\\\ -9x+7y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-3x+y \\\\ -2x-8y \\\\ -9x+7y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b=-2+7=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63300c6c-1cbb-5970-821f-9c46742e51cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270147} {:answer/id #uuid "65b0e9da-992a-5d80-8f54-968f9e9d2e25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270175} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5b7172-d2fa-59ca-b0d7-b05bbb66b915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270660} {:answer/id #uuid "b384b81c-b3c7-54ec-98fd-9c758675d43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270870} {:answer/id #uuid "f3eb5f25-b697-5a85-8d5d-323807fa18c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270147} :answer-field/id #uuid "1399026f-f326-5cca-9ef6-2bee5a08ea69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271543}] :question/id #uuid "fdacaa99-1004-54ca-b9a5-d81789a7f2dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-140422" :question/problem "$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\,T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}5x+4y \\\\ 3y+bx \\\\ -6x+cy\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $c+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5x+4y \\\\ -x+3y \\\\ -6x+7y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5x+4y \\\\ 3y-x \\\\ -6x+7y\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}5x+4y \\\\ 3y+(-1)x \\\\ -6x+(7)y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $c+b=(-1)+7=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360732 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d943f74-7ce4-5666-a56a-6ecd5423e419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358279} {:answer/id #uuid "6938ae13-0505-5a60-b7d6-b915fee009d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358673} {:answer/id #uuid "95859ec9-6557-5778-a40f-14512eb583d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359060} {:answer/id #uuid "cdbabc0a-17f1-575d-bd87-59761b002b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359560} {:answer/id #uuid "e28fbf8b-e75e-58a2-b33b-a80d43d4bcdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359757} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a86ba18-495d-51a6-80ec-a9155903f190" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360232}] :question/id #uuid "53c0832f-dc15-5565-a318-0725a0cdfe01" :question/math-academy-id "q-96974" :question/problem "$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}7x+2y+az \\\\ bx-3z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-3z\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}7x+2y+(-5)z \\\\ 3x-3z\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b=(-5)+3=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3950395c-0c8d-5808-b51f-40f270779488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358257} {:answer/id #uuid "4627f24f-b869-5c20-83aa-cfe354cdc94e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358352} {:answer/id #uuid "63a1edc1-2650-5427-9b41-a6100b8922fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358622} {:answer/id #uuid "b2bf96ea-a13f-50b7-bfef-5b4467f9e6ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359306} {:answer/id #uuid "dccd730a-e90b-528f-ac36-bcf521bc5818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358622} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9411d09-4dcb-5c11-ab45-249223295fc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360410}] :question/id #uuid "7080be8f-7dad-583a-b741-807360c5f79a" :question/math-academy-id "q-96977" :question/problem "$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}ay+3z-x \\\\ bz-2x+cy\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-x+0y+3z \\\\ -2x+4y+2z\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0y+3z-x \\\\ 2z-2x+4y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}0y+3z-x \\\\ 2z-2x+4y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+c=0+2+4=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fb5a88e-2c16-50c0-a11b-1857fef41b83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436051} {:answer/id #uuid "4df16430-0c5c-51d3-b20c-0818ccaee58e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436053} {:answer/id #uuid "89fb8e93-7da5-59dc-a467-6a051fba4e92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436057} {:answer/id #uuid "8db1b7fe-f0f1-5029-831c-002c537419e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436058} {:answer/id #uuid "d4787125-f5f3-5522-b754-798f786e8b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436058} :answer-field/id #uuid "927c6a5b-b400-51f5-ba26-11160c313dcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436069}] :question/id #uuid "93b16baf-60a0-5351-9b6d-e1dbecba8523" :question/math-academy-id "q-96976" :question/problem "$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\,T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3y+ax \\\\ bx+4y \\\\ cy+3x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5x+3y \\\\ -2x+4y \\\\ 3x-y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3y+5x \\\\ -2x+4y \\\\ -y+3x\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3y+5x \\\\ (-2)x+4y \\\\ (-1)y+3x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+c=5+(-2)+(-1)=2.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Components of a Linear Map"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087754 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087570 :question/id #uuid "0ae354ba-19f3-570c-bbfc-56dd5dbbafa8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5519" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](images/46/46bb3e9777a3944eb6b2f458911571442f57a5fae2f7aed1bb924522c51cad4a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088159 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dfef3be-387d-58e0-962e-610c2718c76e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ -19\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085609} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb1de35-1e1a-554e-9d36-73661693b779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085610} {:answer/id #uuid "e366d3e9-74ac-51d8-8ae4-7b4c078eada8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 29\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085611} {:answer/id #uuid "5486f7d0-2731-5874-9202-ec6348c540da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 28\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085612} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea90893-82ca-5ac0-9c99-f0f61ad5c95f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 29\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085613}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b5a25e70-2c66-5a7e-9399-a24f5a637dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085608}] :question/id #uuid "40399821-2d15-5aea-a244-2a9d18bf7b90" :question/math-academy-id "q-38262" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T: R^{3} → R^{2}$, find $T(v)$.\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, v = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "031311d8-4f06-51fe-89d1-8d5c2d6815da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324003} {:answer/id #uuid "04471c6a-0e18-5215-a68a-22f2d933fba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324014} {:answer/id #uuid "1b7fe73c-e86a-54db-9e76-549c68c330d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324205} {:answer/id #uuid "867a5c38-9203-5d24-86f1-a6feddd3fbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325112} {:answer/id #uuid "bab58a11-0363-50e9-a185-aa326bfc8a86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/mat